  "statement": "Every regular edge-transitive graph is vertex-transitive.",
  "definitions": "Finite simple graph; regular = all vertices have the same degree; edge-transitive = Aut(G) acts transitively on the set of unordered edges (NOT arc-transitive); vertex-transitive = Aut(G) acts transitively on V(G).",
  "truth_label": "false",
  "ground_truth_witness": "The Folkman graph on V={0,...,19} with 40 edges, E=[[0,1],[0,5],[0,15],[0,19],[1,2],[1,14],[1,16],[2,3],[2,9],[2,15],[3,4],[3,8],[3,10],[4,5],[4,9],[4,19],[5,6],[5,18],[6,7],[6,13],[6,19],[7,8],[7,12],[7,14],[8,9],[8,13],[9,10],[10,11],[10,17],[11,12],[11,16],[11,18],[12,13],[12,17],[13,14],[14,15],[15,16],[16,17],[17,18],[18,19]] (equivalently the LCF code [5,-7,-7,5]^5). It is 4-regular and Aut (order 3840) is transitive on the 40 edges, but it has two vertex orbits of size 10, so it is not vertex-transitive; it is the smallest semisymmetric graph.",
